[D — THE DIMENSION TELL: the triangle holds its detune, a sine does not]
      The pitch offset IS the delay slope. For a TRIANGLE the slope is a SQUARE
      wave: the detune sits at exactly +-c and only flips sign at the apexes. For a
      SINE the slope is a sine, whose value distribution is the ARCSINE law, so the
      detune sweeps continuously through every value including zero. Closed-form
      predictions for a sine, which is what makes this a real test and not a
      threshold: P(|c| > 0.8 peak) = 1 - (2/pi)asin(0.8) = 0.410 and
      P(|c| < 0.1 peak) = (2/pi)asin(0.1) = 0.064. A flat-topped trapezoid — the
      shape an earlier draft of the bible specced — would drive the SECOND number
      toward its flat-top duty cycle, i.e. the detune would periodically DROP OUT.
      TRIANGLE (Two Line)  peak  120.0 cents · mass at |c|>0.8pk 0.988 · at |c|<0.1pk 0.001
      SINE     (Tremble)   peak  449.7 cents · mass at |c|>0.8pk 0.501 · at |c|<0.1pk 0.055
      arcsine prediction for a sine:                             0.410              0.064
  ok    triangle detune is BIMODAL: >= 90 % of the time at +-peak 0.988 of samples at |c| > 0.8 peak
  ok    triangle has NO zero dwell (a flat top would put one there) 0.0010 of samples at |c| < 0.1 peak
  ok    the SINE A/B proves the metric can see a non-square slope sine lobe mass 0.501 (arcsine predicts 0.410)
