[F — THE WHOLE MATRIX: EVERY KNOB SWEPT 0->100 ON EVERY TYPE]
      🔴 fb425 — THE FULL-MATRIX LAW. fb422 swept 12 knobs x 6 Types = 72 cells and
      called Law 1 proved. It was not: `sweep()` never took a CHARACTER, so all 72
      cells ran on Character 0 and the other 7/8 of the matrix had never been
      measured once. 12 knobs x 6 Types x 8 Characters = 576 cells, and all 576 are
      gated here, each on its own line. Every metric is read off the OUTPUT.
      Each knob carries its own ABSOLUTE audible-step floor — 'no plateau' cannot be a
      fraction of the span, because one huge step at the bottom would then excuse every
      dead quarter after it.
      🔑 EVERY CELL ALSO GETS A BIT-IDENTITY PROBE, and that one is not a judgement
      call: knob 0 % and knob 100 % are run through the same engine on the same noise
      and the sample vectors are compared EXACTLY. Bit-identical is a FAILURE unless
      the cell is named in the KNOWN-INERT ROSTER below with a reason — and that table
      is asserted to a fixed size AND checked in reverse, so a cell cannot be declared
      inert and then quietly come alive (or be used to hide a live-but-deaf knob).

