      B · THE ANTI-HAAS CLAUSE. The refutation's signature was that all six R11
          numbers came out IDENTICAL TO THREE DECIMALS, because they were reading a
          trigonometric identity rather than six different machines. A ceiling gate
          that cannot tell the Types apart is not measuring the device, so this one
          asserts that it can: the four pitch Types must differ by >= 15 % of the
          largest, and the two phase Types must differ from them by construction
          (carrier mass 1.000 vs << 1).
