[J — MONO FOLD-DOWN, per Type, per Field, and per tagged Character]
      GATE: at MIX 1.0 (no dry to sum with) the time-AVERAGED mono magnitude
      spectrum must stay within 4 dB of dry in every log band, and the mono RMS
      within 3 dB. Mix 0.5 was tried first and measures the wrong thing: an
      equal-power crossfade of two CORRELATED signals is +3 dB by arithmetic, so
      `Bands` — whose mono fold is the input BIT FOR BIT — read +3.14 dB and
      "failed". The averaging matters too: a MOVING comb must average out, which
      is why magSpec averages 12 hops across the probe.
